NAME
       vgreduce - remove physical volumes from a volume group

SYNOPSIS
       vgreduce VG PV...
       vgreduce -a VG
       vgreduce --removemissing VG

DESCRIPTION
       vgreduce takes physical volumes out of a volume group. A PV can leave
       only when none of its extents are used; move the data off it first
       with pvmove (when the other PVs have room). Afterwards the device is
       still a PV but belongs to no group; pvremove clears it.

OPTIONS
       -a, --all
              Remove every PV that has no used extents.

       --removemissing
              Forget PVs whose disk has disappeared.

       -f, --force
              Go ahead without some checks.

EXAMPLES
           pvmove /dev/vdc1
           vgreduce vgdata /dev/vdc1
           pvremove /dev/vdc1

SEE ALSO
       vgextend(8), pvmove(8), pvremove(8), pvs(8)
